{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqivmpsymqf","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"OpenCode prompt and workspace parity gap","summary":"Current OpenCode plugin docs/types (OpenCode 1.17.8, docs last updated June 17 2026) expose project plugins under `.opencode/plugins`, `event`, `tool.execute.before`, custom `tool`, and a `chat.message` hook with `sessionID`. Zonoid's OpenCode bridge currently registers lifecycle, gates tool writes, mints `task_create`, and schedules wakeups, but it does not POST `/workspace` on plugin/session startup and does not use `chat.message` to call `/classify` and append Claude/Codex-style prompt context. That leaves prompt injection and workspace binding below Claude/Codex parity.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-18T02:24:29.986Z","vec":[-0.08867663890123367,-0.07648315280675888,-0.029177287593483925,0.05462806299328804,-0.013871071860194206,-0.058354854583740234,0.009482543915510178,0.025678062811493874,-0.002806966658681631,-0.021627947688102722,-0.003037369577214122,-0.041471581906080246,-0.08598141372203827,0.06388455629348755,0.08647557348012924,0.09001951664686203,0.0032952376641333103,-0.09806938469409943,0.05418426916003227,0.040318623185157776,0.032394424080848694,0.015827491879463196,0.0563952773809433,-0.013640126213431358,0.00894973985850811,0.0002904106804635376,0.008689500391483307,0.031222904101014137,0.0762840211391449,0.052532996982336044,0.05311013385653496,0.060960035771131516,0.05776025354862213,-0.019970592111349106,0.07085246592760086,0.08350831270217896,0.11531194299459457,-0.002162589691579342,-0.03982871398329735,-0.04791273921728134,0.029490366578102112,-0.004313573706895113,-0.04333028569817543,0.06246112287044525,-0.03358708694577217,-0.02225710265338421,0.015186445787549019,-0.07832503318786621,-0.09354689717292786,-0.03820297122001648,0.041720543056726456,-0.05014185607433319,0.04792184755206108,0.055497314780950546,0.010117997415363789,0.009669229388237,-0.025296738371253014,0.037829652